<section class="section">
      

      <div class="container narrow reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">The Story Behind the Name</p>

        <h1>Meet Professor Jerry</h1>

        <p class="lead">
          Some people are born builders. Others are born teachers.
          Jerry has spent his life doing both.
        </p>

        <div class="about-portrait">
          <img src="/assets/images/professorjerry.png" alt="Professor Jerry" loading="lazy">
        </div>

        <p>
          After earning bachelor's and master's degrees in Electrical
          Engineering at the University of Texas at Austin, Jerry joined IBM, where he spent 31 years, retiring as a
          Senior Software Architect. During that time, he traveled
          throughout the United States and around the world, helping
          customers understand complex technology through technical
          seminars, product demonstrations, and hands-on training.
        </p>

        <p>
          When he retired from IBM, teaching remained a natural calling.
          Jerry joined the McCombs School of Business at The University
          of Texas at Austin as a professor of Information Technology.
          It was there that students first began calling him
          <strong>"Professor Jerry"</strong>&mdash;a name that has followed
          him ever since.
        </p>

        <div class="about-rv-story">
          <!-- Save the campsite illustration as jerry-penney-rv.png in assets/images. -->
          <figure class="about-rv-photo">
            <img src="/assets/images/jerrypenneyrv.png"
              alt="Cartoon illustration of Jerry and Penney in front of their travel trailer" width="1672" height="941"
              loading="lazy">
          </figure>

          <p>
            In 2025, Jerry and his wife, Penney, purchased their first travel
            trailer and discovered what millions of RV owners already
            know: owning an RV is both incredibly rewarding and
            surprisingly complex. During their first year and a half,
            they traveled more than 13,000 miles while learning firsthand
            what it means to own, maintain, troubleshoot, and enjoy an RV.
          </p>

          <p>
            Instead of simply accepting the learning curve, Jerry did
            what engineers do&mdash;he immersed himself in it.
          </p>
        </div>

        <p>
          He attended the National RV Training Academy, earning
          certification as a Registered RV Technician. Wanting to go
          even further, he completed the National RV Inspectors Academy
          and became a Certified RV Inspector in June 2026.
        </p>

        <p>
          Coming from a family of educators, Jerry has always believed
          that the best way to help someone is to teach them
          <strong>why</strong> something works&mdash;not just
          <strong>how</strong> to fix it.
        </p>

        <p>
          Today, Professor Jerry combines decades of engineering
          experience, a lifetime of teaching, and nationally recognized
          RV certifications to help RV owners become more confident,
          more knowledgeable, and ultimately enjoy their RVs with
          fewer surprises.
        </p>

        <p>
          Whether you're buying your first RV, learning how its systems
          work, or trying to solve a frustrating problem, Professor
          Jerry's goal is simple:
        </p>

        <blockquote>
          <strong>Helping RV Owners Understand Their RV With Confidence.</strong>
        </blockquote>
      </div>
    </section>
